    "bonded": "Separate rod beams; exact six-DOF eccentric ties",
    "sleeve": "Separate rod beams; circular-clearance frictionless compression-only contact; free axial slip and spin"
  },
  "root_boundary": "All six shell and rod root DOFs clamped; integral sleeves rigidly follow shell cross-section; bonded module seams",
  "scope_limit": "Small-displacement models only. The finite-rotation single-beam solver refuses rods. No friction, glue strength, bearing/crushing, dry seams or experimental aircraft validation.",
  "references": {
    "bonded": "Euler-Bernoulli composite EI = EI_carrier + 2*Erod*(Irod+Arod*offset^2), symmetric rods at z=+/-10 mm; tip=P L^3/(3 EI).",
    "sleeve": "Two independent cantilever compliances ks=3EI/L^3, kr=3ErIr/L^3. Before contact w=P/ks; after contact w=(P+sign(P)*kr*gap)/(ks+kr). Continuous prismatic sleeve has the same exact solution because the relative cubic profile is below gap at every interior station."
  },
